{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong","id":433151,"title":"in dark ages devil due are all demons equally strong?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-08T14:45:38-07:00","id":433151,"title":"in dark ages devil due are all demons equally strong?","content":"overall i liked the book a lot more than demon the fallen but this seems like an issue<br /> ok, i may be reading this wrong but as i see it most demons(torment 10) have the exact same amount of arcana. you can add taints and pacts but the point is that everyone may do it.<br /> that is if im a player with willpower of 10 a maximum amount of pacts and torment 9 im just slightly behind belial or lucifer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T13:19:30-07:00","id":448150,"title":"","content":"I think you need to take a different POV in terms of what &quot;power&quot; is/can be, Mark. Cross-example: Tremere wasn't the most competent of mages in the OoH (by Magister Mundi standards), in life, nor was he the most mystically talented after the change in 1022 (much of his power is based solely on his being 3rd generation via Saulot); what he *was*, however, was extremely cunning, charismatic and manipulative, and *that* went a long way towards making shit happen and giving him the status he had. Similar thing with Lucifer, et al. -- it is entirely possible for your demon to have a similar degree of mystical might compared to the &quot;big names&quot;, but he likely doesn't have the same degree of metaphysical/meta-social status/influence that the others do. It's not simply a question of stats and dots, but fluff as well. (Also, remember a critical metaphysical point: in The Void, *all* demons possess unlimited spiritual power, well beyond anything even the most vaunted mages or Anti's possess/demonstrate; the stats and dots in the game represent how much of that power/ability a given demon can bring to bear -- or even remember -- in the Physical/Umbral worlds... don't use that to gauge what extra-meta-physical power/influence they may have/wield in ways and on levels that the mortal mind can barely grasp... It's much more abstract and complicated than that, and not something understood by dots, but by fluff...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T06:58:25-07:00","id":449148,"title":"","content":"it's just that it doesn't fit the fact that the archdukes are supposed to be strong enough to reduce creation to ashes... if only they cooperated.<br /> <br /> im not sure where it says that all demons possess unlimited spiritual power in or outside the abyss/oblivion . this does go against the established lore.<br /> <br /> for instance asmodeus and abaddon pretty much fucked the war effort precisely because asmodeus had a vision of humanity using their divine potential(true magick) to enslave manking and he sought to prevent this.<br /> for the fallen did not have god/s the one's/power while he granted said power to humans.<br /> <br /> tremere's case is complicated. it is my personal conviction that he may have had a weak avatar as blood treachery says &quot;he was limited by happenstance&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T14:14:44-07:00","id":449762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=449148#post449148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's just that it doesn't fit the fact that the archdukes are supposed to be strong enough to reduce creation to ashes... if only they cooperated.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't the sort of thing you assign dots to portray. Archdukes might be that powerful, but the how and whys of their world-ending cooperation is what matters, not the raw stats each individual Archduke has. Just like Just John said, the dangers presented by powerful demons comes from something more ineffable that what can be easily portrayed on a sheet.<br /> <br /> The Archdukes might be able to bring creation to its knees, but they aren't going to do it by rolling a big fat dice pool. It is going to happen through storytelling.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T15:29:44-07:00","id":449834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=449762#post449762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That isn't the sort of thing you assign dots to portray. Archdukes might be that powerful, but the how and whys of their world-ending cooperation is what matters, not the raw stats each individual Archduke has. Just like Just John said, the dangers presented by powerful demons comes from something more ineffable that what can be easily portrayed on a sheet.<br /> <br /> The Archdukes might be able to bring creation to its knees, but they aren't going to do it by rolling a big fat dice pool. It is going to happen through storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>EXACTLY.<br /> <br /> Mark: much like with trying to understand the balance factor between the dots/mechanics, and the fluff, for understanding Pillars in DA:M (vis-a-vis the various threads we've been discussing things in), the dots/mechanics, alone, don't tell the entire story when it comes to the power of demons, especially relative to each other. Fluff is every bit as important. And there's nothing counter-indicative about demons possessing nigh-unlimited spiritual power in The Void Outside of Creation (Jehovah's Garden) -- in Real Life(tm), that shit is straight-up old-school Qaballah wherein Jehovah (God, as we might understand him/it/the entity) is but one of many such beings; many of the &quot;demons&quot; that are alluded to are not &quot;fallen angels&quot;, as such (though many/most are), but rather other entities such as Jehovah, himself, who are attempting to enter his &quot;garden&quot; (read: Creation/Reality(tm) as we understand it, including most levels of the various Umbrae), either out of a desire for power/influence, or simply out of curiosity/nosiness. While Devil's Due, of course, takes a more &quot;flatline&quot; approach, it doesn't invalidate other concepts that have been laid down for (D)emons, across the various lines of WoD books, but merely delineates many facets/factors in a more integral way that is a touch more incorporated, relative to the other splats, than had been previously published (and DO NOT get me started on D:tF -- anyone who knows me at all/any of my post-history knows that I have a very bad taste in my mouth for that book...).<br /> <br /> And a metaphysical point that should be kept in mind: while most demons have essentially unlimited spiritual power outside of &quot;creation&quot;, they don't have the ability to &quot;do anything&quot; with it while in The Void, and their ability to bring such power to bear in Creation(tm) is limited by the amount of Faith that they can glean from others (For comparative purposes, their &quot;unlimited strength&quot; only really becomes a game-mechanic thing when, say, a given mage/what-have-you actually reaches into The Void to directly deal with said demon(s) on his/their direct terms/home turf... and there aren't <i>nearly</i> enough dots in Avatar/Arete to save <b>any</b> mage at that point.... #YouAreFucked ) That aspect cannot be stressed enough. It's entirely possible for a given demon, depending on time/space/influence, to wield much more power in Creation(tm) than Lucifer directly can, simply based on circumstances and ready belief/corruption of others. That in no way invalidates the meta-concept/truth that Lucifer is still superior to said demon, and will whoop said demon's (metaphysical) ass in any direct confrontation -- it just demonstrates how the power of demons is, quite literally, multi-dimensional, and the power/stats indicated for how they interact *here* doesn't necessarily apply to the more abstract levels where they exist &quot;over there&quot;.<br /> <br /> Seriously, for as truly metaphysically mind-bendy as (D)emon lore is, it was never really laid out that well in... okay... I was about to violate my own prohibition from above... gonna spend a Willpower and avoid slipping into MechaStreisand form and demolishing a given town in Colorado... &gt;deep breath&lt;<br /> <br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <br /> In any case, the general rules/guidelines in DD is actually better than anything else published for demons in CWoD, even if it isn't perfect. It has enough right/on-the-button that it can tooled with and made fine. Remember: dots/mechanics are only one-half of the equation (just like for Pillars in DA:M) -- an important thing, true, and not to be disregarded, but still only one side of the coin. The Fluff is the other half (as is simply having a good grasp of the metaphysics and concepts involved, which is something no scaling, of any kind, can convey), and that, too, is every bit as important as the other half. When the two are used together, as they're meant to, all things become much, much clearer...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T17:25:27-07:00","id":449912,"title":"","content":"Mark,<br /> <br /> How familiar are you with Demon the Fallen? Since Devil's Due definitely has some articulation with DtF on many levels (vide even having &quot;Torment&quot; as a thing...), perhaps there might be some answers there? <br /> <br /> According to DtF, pretty much every demon you see in DA is going to be an Earthbound or just-about-to-be-an-Earthbound. ALL Earthbound have Torment 10. If they don't now, they will. Damn quick. It doesn't diminish their MASSIVE levels of power that they can bring to bear, especially if they have been caught &quot;above ground&quot; for any prolonged period of time. They don't have the Archdukes with stats, but, if they did, they would have Torment 10. That's a guarantee. As will po-dunk Demon Fred who was just summoned from the Void (that's the CWOD/DtF Void, the prison created for the demons for being uppity, not some ineffable &quot;outside the creation of Biggest Angel&quot; void) using some degraded iteration of Lucifer's ritual. Since demons summoned to Earth in DA don't get the &quot;cushion&quot; the Fallen get when they merge with mortals (not possess), arguably they are Torment 10 from the get go. (A modern Fallen with Torment less than 10 that becomes an Earthbound gains Torment hand over fist when they loose the &quot;human factor&quot;) DD doesn't handle Torment in exactly the same way, but it doesn't exactly handle demons at the level that Earthbound tries to tackle either. Not that Earthbound really tackles the Archdukes or Ba'al, but it gives some scope of what the stats can be like for ancient insidious profane evils that are LESS powerful than the big 5(ish) and THOSE &quot;little&quot; guys are really really badass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T23:21:13-07:00","id":450198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=449834#post449834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EXACTLY.<br /> <br /> Mark: much like with trying to understand the balance factor between the dots/mechanics, and the fluff, for understanding Pillars in DA:M (vis-a-vis the various threads we've been discussing things in), the dots/mechanics, alone, don't tell the entire story when it comes to the power of demons, especially relative to each other. Fluff is every bit as important. And there's nothing counter-indicative about demons possessing nigh-unlimited spiritual power in The Void Outside of Creation (Jehovah's Garden) -- in Real Life(tm), that shit is straight-up old-school Qaballah wherein Jehovah (God, as we might understand him/it/the entity) is but one of many such beings; many of the &quot;demons&quot; that are alluded to are not &quot;fallen angels&quot;, as such (though many/most are), but rather other entities such as Jehovah, himself, who are attempting to enter his &quot;garden&quot; (read: Creation/Reality(tm) as we understand it, including most levels of the various Umbrae), either out of a desire for power/influence, or simply out of curiosity/nosiness. While Devil's Due, of course, takes a more &quot;flatline&quot; approach, it doesn't invalidate other concepts that have been laid down for (D)emons, across the various lines of WoD books, but merely delineates many facets/factors in a more integral way that is a touch more incorporated, relative to the other splats, than had been previously published (and DO NOT get me started on D:tF -- anyone who knows me at all/any of my post-history knows that I have a very bad taste in my mouth for that book...).<br /> <br /> And a metaphysical point that should be kept in mind: while most demons have essentially unlimited spiritual power outside of &quot;creation&quot;, they don't have the ability to &quot;do anything&quot; with it while in The Void, and their ability to bring such power to bear in Creation(tm) is limited by the amount of Faith that they can glean from others (For comparative purposes, their &quot;unlimited strength&quot; only really becomes a game-mechanic thing when, say, a given mage/what-have-you actually reaches into The Void to directly deal with said demon(s) on his/their direct terms/home turf... and there aren't <i>nearly</i> enough dots in Avatar/Arete to save <b>any</b> mage at that point.... #YouAreFucked ) That aspect cannot be stressed enough. It's entirely possible for a given demon, depending on time/space/influence, to wield much more power in Creation(tm) than Lucifer directly can, simply based on circumstances and ready belief/corruption of others. That in no way invalidates the meta-concept/truth that Lucifer is still superior to said demon, and will whoop said demon's (metaphysical) ass in any direct confrontation -- it just demonstrates how the power of demons is, quite literally, multi-dimensional, and the power/stats indicated for how they interact *here* doesn't necessarily apply to the more abstract levels where they exist &quot;over there&quot;.<br /> <br /> Seriously, for as truly metaphysically mind-bendy as (D)emon lore is, it was never really laid out that well in... okay... I was about to violate my own prohibition from above... gonna spend a Willpower and avoid slipping into MechaStreisand form and demolishing a given town in Colorado... &gt;deep breath&lt;<br /> <br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <br /> In any case, the general rules/guidelines in DD is actually better than anything else published for demons in CWoD, even if it isn't perfect. It has enough right/on-the-button that it can tooled with and made fine. Remember: dots/mechanics are only one-half of the equation (just like for Pillars in DA:M) -- an important thing, true, and not to be disregarded, but still only one side of the coin. The Fluff is the other half (as is simply having a good grasp of the metaphysics and concepts involved, which is something no scaling, of any kind, can convey), and that, too, is every bit as important as the other half. When the two are used together, as they're meant to, all things become much, much clearer...</div> </div> </div> </div>to be honest i only know very little about the kabbalah. only the sephirothic tree plus the idea of qlippothic universe.. i think i saw sth simiar to your idea of gardens in revelations of the dark mother. or some other book. though i interpreted it to mean &quot;realms in the umbra&quot;. it fits lilith being the very first mage.<br /> <br /> by creation you mean the tellurian right?<br /> <br /> as for demons aren't most of the beings that are called demons beings of this world? banes are corrupt entropy spirits. spectres are formwer wraiths. the yama kings are, well the only requirement is to own rea estane in thr 1000 hells.<br /> i suppose a case could be made about hive demons as well as certain high ranking astral umbrood(Implied to be merely masquerading as demons as we understand them)<br /> depending on whether you see the deep umbra(curiously also called the void sometimes) as part of the tellurian.<br /> <br /> the abyss(at least from what books like guide to low clans say) is propably synonymous with obivion or the void outside creation that seeks to devour creation.<br /> <br /> on a separate note one book(rogue council i think) seems to agree with the idea of jehovah being just one god. as it talks a lot about a demiurge essentially taking the place of the one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 03-20-2015, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T03:52:28-07:00","id":450284,"title":"","content":"Ha. If you had a hard time thinking about how WoD cosmologies interact, just try seeing what Demon has to say on the topic. Usually gives me migraines due to the high horse the writers were on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T04:14:32-07:00","id":450290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=450198#post450198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as for demons aren't most of the beings that are called demons beings of this world? banes are corrupt entropy spirits. spectres are formwer wraiths. the yama kings are, well the only requirement is to own rea estane in thr 1000 hells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actuallly No they aren't. At least not from the stand point of Demon the Fallen and Devil's Due. In DtF and D'sD (Keep in mind D'sD is meant to be a supplement to the Dark Age line, not a full on game line like DtF) The &quot;Demons&quot; are of from &quot;outside&quot; of this Reality and not from it. and more then that, they actually &quot;predate&quot; Reality...they were around and in existance BEFORE Reality even existed.<br /> <br /> Those you named: The Banes, Entropy Spirit, Specters and Yama King are more recent and are from &quot;within&quot; Reality and are actually younger the Reality. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T04:18:54-07:00","id":450294,"title":"","content":"let me try this. from a dtf perspective the wyrm/ebon dragon and the wyld are angels. the weaver is propably lucifer(?)<br /> <br /> and before anyone says that this is imposing christianity on the whole world,this is only partially true.<br /> for instance i sincerely doubt that lucifer was called lucifer back then. i mean ,seriously,latin?<br /> <br /> names like nergal or erashnigal are far older than the abrahamic religions and it's stated that the earth bound for the most part just masqueraded as the gods.<br /> they propably inflate their influence on history. they did not run rome. at least not any more than the eternal senate or the cult of mercury or the mithraic singers did.<br /> sort of how today's vampires think that they ruled during the dark ages. people have a tendency to look at past eras as ideal.<br /> <br /> it's just that the name lucifer bears some(possibly consensus backed) resonance with the specific spirit. in the same way that the earthbound were warped by the beliefs of their followers.<br /> <br /> if i say lucifer,iblis,heylel, eosforos, or amatsu-mikaboshi it won't make any difference. <br /> <br /> as for the umbrood i think it's explicitly stated that the incarna created all of the rest of them. or at least most.<br /> <br /> thus at least some of the celestines/incarna might be seen as elohim or similar spirits of balance.<br /> <br /> the neverborn/children(?) are NOT the fallen. they are propably a separate aspect of telos/god/whatever.<br /> <br /> the yama kings are a group of different beings though they may or may not retain distinctions. a few of the originals may indeed be called &quot;angels&quot; like the ainu related yama king.<br /> <br /> though im not sure if any gameline book has given any explicit info on the nature of the one or the tellurian or tellurians(depending on your intepretation of what prime 9 does as well asthe wheel of ages. as i wrote before we must account the possibility of a false demiurge.) or ascension or armageddon and many more plot holes.<br /> <br /> changelings/fae tuathe de dannan/wyck/aliens.... i have no idea .<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T07:50:45-07:00","id":450434,"title":"","content":"No. Demon's worse then that, and it's the only line that completely and unequivocally explains how all of Existance works. It does it by pissing over Werewolf, Mage, Changeling, Wraith and even Vampire to an extent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T09:12:37-07:00","id":450512,"title":"","content":"doesn't mage do sth similar? albeit it's less blatant.<br /> <br /> plus in demon the fallen it's implied that many of these things are just speculations. <br /> <br /> and they are not incompatible.<br /> <br /> for instance. at many points it implies a consensual reality. mage and dtf fit together very well i believe. their is afterall such a thing as cosmological constants. hell they even share enochian with the order of hermes and i bet some eastern demons may use kaja.<br /> 2. it's heavily implied that demons memories are.. clouded to say the least plus influenced by their human host.plus before their rebellion they were little more than beings doing a specific job. so many of the things they know may be assumptions.<br /> 3.the fera basically say that some big spirit created them. the demons agree. does it matter if we call it gaia or emerald mother or whatever?<br /> 4. im not sure how they piss of changeling. maybe it's because im not familiar with the game.<br /> 5.vampires(most anyway) believe in the caine thing. demons agree. though it's worth noting that gaviel is actually an evil demon and also propably speaks in metaphorically some times.<br /> for instance i highly doubt(and some books do imply it i think) that there were just 2 humans at the time of the rebellion.<br /> 6. many so called pagan religions do have a belief in a single creator. so long as you look far enough in the past. it 's just that it's not relevant anymore.<br /> 7.fera say the weaver made monotheistic religions.. assuming this is to be taken literally this does reinforce my idea that the weaver is lucifer. again does it matter if we call it weaver or lucifer or phoenix(per dragons of the east.)<br /> 8.the idea that the fallen physically created all of stygia up to and including the labyrinth and harrowing is indeed stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T09:22:18-07:00","id":450517,"title":"","content":"Well, according to them, they physically created EVERYTHING (barring a few surprises, like the Abyss, and some things they never thought about much, like where the where was before they started working and was there anything already there before they started working), so, of course they created the Shadowlands. Just like they built the mountains, the sky, the stars, space, time, comfort, love, bugs + everything mentioned in the &quot;Everything is Awesome&quot; song&quot;) They kinda HAD to. Death was built into creation, after all, there's supposed to be &quot;rest&quot; on the final day. So they had death, which correlates to having the dead, and, since death is a thing of the flesh, they needed to have some place for the rest (e.g. the spirit) of the now-dead being to go... or else render all of Creation relatively untidy with an increasing accumulation of ghosts. Apparently Charon (the Angel) was a neat freak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T12:19:59-07:00","id":450684,"title":"","content":"Wait, does DtF actually come out and say that the members of the Triat, the vast beings that underlie the Tellurian, are just angels or demons? Blagh. I know that the Paradise Lost narrative was never made to play nice with the other cosmologies of the WoD, but if that is the approach they took, it is riotously stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T12:34:57-07:00","id":450702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=450684#post450684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, does DtF actually come out and say that the members of the Triat, the vast beings that underlie the Tellurian, are just angels or demons? Blagh. I know that the Paradise Lost narrative was never made to play nice with the other cosmologies of the WoD, but if that is the approach they took, it is riotously stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> lucifer says that the 2 creators of the imbued are angels. a hunter books calls them the ebon dragon and scarlet empress beings 2 ministers of creation. the ebon dragon is the wyrm and the scarlet empress is the wyld. i would also like to point out that this proves that (a few things aside) dtf is not so abrahamic as people think it is.<br /> lucifer was propably not intended to be seen as the weaver. it's a personal hypothesis of mine.<br /> <br /> ziana is gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T13:46:02-07:00","id":450807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=450684#post450684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, does DtF actually come out and say that the members of the Triat, the vast beings that underlie the Tellurian, are just angels or demons? Blagh. I know that the Paradise Lost narrative was never made to play nice with the other cosmologies of the WoD, but if that is the approach they took, it is riotously stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the way that DtF doesn't deal with the Umbra at all in a functional way, for reasons that both make sense internally and make no sense as well, the Triat doesn't even register to them. <br /> <br /> Effectively, all Incarne, the Triat, Gaia, those are things of the Spirit World. A Fallen would probably be appalled at their existence, as they are symptomatic of the fact the world broke and all sorts of things are less than they were (meaning the spirit aspect isn't a part of the functional whole and seems, to their point of view, to just have disappeared) Demons look at the earth and feel like it's just a pale shadow of what it should be. To them Gaia and the physical world should be one and the same, existing simlutaneously in a reality where all the layers are in play at the same time. <br /> <br /> Of course, that conveniently ignores WHO exactly it was that is responsible for breaking the world. (Which is them) Or for the fact that said Demons are also just reduced pale imitations of their former selves shoved into an emotionally dead human sleeve. So what the hell do they know? <br /> <br /> If that's ridiculously stupid, then okay, but Vampire doesn't deal with the Triat at all. Either does Wraith. Or Changeling. It works a smidge better in Mage, but, all told, Mages seem to ignore the Triat if it doesn't work for them, just say the Werewolves are being overly animistic and hanging identities on forces that transcend such things or buy in to the degree appropriate to their paradigm. If the Triat HAS to exist as the fundamental underpinning of the cosmos for all the games, it's just privileging the mythology of Werewolf and slopping that all over the other games. Which is doing exactly the same thing people say Demon does.... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T13:48:36-07:00","id":450817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=450702#post450702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> lucifer says that the 2 creators of the imbued are angels. a hunter books calls them the ebon dragon and scarlet empress beings 2 ministers of creation. the ebon dragon is the wyrm and the scarlet empress is the wyld. i would also like to point out that this proves that (a few things aside) dtf is not so abrahamic as people think it is.<br /> lucifer was propably not intended to be seen as the weaver. it's a personal hypothesis of mine.<br /> <br /> ziana is gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do have a location for where they say the Ebon Dragon and the Scarlet Empress are equivalent to the Wyrm and the Wyld? I haven't seen that connection. I thought it was more that they were Gabriel and Raphael (?, I think?), the only two loyal angels who did not &quot;transcend&quot; at the end of the War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T14:00:33-07:00","id":450843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=450807#post450807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering the way that DtF doesn't deal with the Umbra at all in a functional way, for reasons that both make sense internally and make no sense as well, the Triat doesn't even register to them.<br /> <br /> Effectively, all Incarne, the Triat, Gaia, those are things of the Spirit World. A Fallen would probably be appalled at their existence, as they are symptomatic of the fact the world broke and all sorts of things are less than they were (meaning the spirit aspect isn't a part of the functional whole and seems, to their point of view, to just have disappeared) Demons look at the earth and feel like it's just a pale shadow of what it should be. To them Gaia and the physical world should be one and the same, existing simlutaneously in a reality where all the layers are in play at the same time.<br /> <br /> Of course, that conveniently ignores WHO exactly it was that is responsible for breaking the world. (Which is them) Or for the fact that said Demons are also just reduced pale imitations of their former selves shoved into an emotionally dead human sleeve. So what the hell do they know?<br /> <br /> If that's ridiculously stupid, then okay, but Vampire doesn't deal with the Triat at all. Either does Wraith. Or Changeling. It works a smidge better in Mage, but, all told, Mages seem to ignore the Triat if it doesn't work for them, just say the Werewolves are being overly animistic and hanging identities on forces that transcend such things or buy in to the degree appropriate to their paradigm. If the Triat HAS to exist as the fundamental underpinning of the cosmos for all the games, it's just privileging the mythology of Werewolf and slopping that all over the other games. Which is doing exactly the same thing people say Demon does....</div> </div> </div> </div>It could also be that all of the games don't actually take place in the same setting. As an aside, I'd also say that Vampire, Mage and Demon often deserve to get slopped over to drive that point home, especially since most of 2nd edition seemed purpose-built for slopping all over Werewolf, principally for the overhyping of Vampire and Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T16:46:24-07:00","id":450995,"title":"","content":"When Demon cosmology and concepts come into discussion, ever since I forced myself to read it way back when it came out my default response is...<br /> <br /> LA LA LA LA LA LA LA LA LA! I cannot hear you! I have no idea what you're talking about and there was never a game called Demon for WoD. If you need Demons, check out Book of the Wyrm, Book Of Madness, Infernalism: Path of Screams and the Baali.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:04:14-07:00","id":451054,"title":"","content":"Which works just find if your are playing Werewolf, Mage or Vampire.<br /> <br /> But Mark seems to be asking about an opponent book for DA Vampire that draws on some of the concepts of DtF with questions that directly bear on issues straight out of DtF, specifically the archdukes of Hell. So the cosmology of Demon is germane to the discussion, probably much more germane than the cosmology of Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Though DtF is pretty heavy handed, (to the point of OMG did they REALLY just denigrate the figures of an actual religion that is being practiced), it's cosmology doesn't necessarily cross-over in a non-mutually exclusive manner with Vampire or Wraith or Reckoning (or with a bit more stretching KoE).<br /> <br /> If you take Mage, tilt it at the right angle and look through these glasses (gives strange looking glasses) and hum along with this song (hands over iPod with ear buds) that might work too.<br /> <br /> Changeling neither integrates or fails to integrate with other lines on a case by case basis, but usually they are so off tripping in their own shared headspace that it doesn't matter overmuch.<br /> <br /> The one cosmology which seems like it has to be absolutely true for the integral pieces of that game to function as it is presented is Werewolf. For Werewolf to work, it really ALL has to be about what's going down with the Triat. So everyone else has to fit into one of these three categories or some mash-up of them... When other games are handled with Werewolf, they have to take into account, usually take on, this absolutist view. I haven't seen nearly as many people trying to shoehorn Werewolf into the other games, it's always seemed like it's trying to take Werewolf's version of things and shoehorn in the other games. (How is Oblivion at part of the Wyrm? Mage Essences are just reflective of the Triat, etc. etc.) It's very seldom the other way around. (So the Wyrm is just a renegade Neverborn or something that crawled out of the Deep Umbra and got stuck in the Middle Umbra or that the werewolves are just obsessed with a trio of aspected powerful Middle Umbra Spirits that seem to line up with the different types of Avatar, etc.)<br /> <br /> DtF just says the Werewolf is wrong, that the Garou are limited and don't know what they're talking about. Like when Garou tell Kindred that Caine story is BS and they are all Wyrm tainted animated corpses. <br /> <br /> It would be simpler if all the game lines were really separated out, but there are so many crossover products, like this one, that sometimes you have to try to figure out what to do when worlds collide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 03-20-2015, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T01:25:03-07:00","id":451371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=450817#post450817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do have a location for where they say the Ebon Dragon and the Scarlet Empress are equivalent to the Wyrm and the Wyld? I haven't seen that connection. I thought it was more that they were Gabriel and Raphael (?, I think?), the only two loyal angels who did not &quot;transcend&quot; at the end of the War.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> dragons of the east. though even before that the connections are obvious other than the fact that the splats of the wod never reachedd an agreement on whether the wyrm is evil.<br /> fera say it's evil. kuei jin and eastern mages think is good. mummies(though it may be obivion they fight not the wyrm, oblivion being some useless thing unlike entropy) say it's bad. setites think it's good. after all their philosoph is like social entropy.<br /> <br /> again does it even matter if we call them gabriel ,raphael, ebon dragon,male or female?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T04:50:02-07:00","id":451426,"title":"","content":"That's not... Do I actually have to type this again? Wyrm is a cosmic principle. It simply is. It always will be and it will be the force of ending, renewal and making the way for new things. If the Wyrm was not actually fulfilling its main purpose, everything on the planet would not exist... there would be no death, no circle of life and the reality would look like a horrifying calcified fixture with pockets of random chaos that would splurt out.<br /> <br /> In addition to this, a facet of the Wyrm is deeply and horribly messed up. It was caused either by Weaver's encroachment or its own attempts at control, but either way there is a part of the Wyrm as a cosmic principle that has a raging hard on to murder, debase and horrifyingly destroy everything in its path. This part is the &quot;evil&quot; that we encunter in Werewolf and why the shifters have issues with the Wyrm. You will note that a lot of shifters have positive things to say about the Wyrm, and that there are even factions who actually serve the sane part of the Wyrm. This gets drowned out in the simplification of everything Wyrmish being evil, which is often conflated by people who are new at Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Also, everything in Werewolf is NOT about the Triat. The Triat simply is. Not every element of the setting stems from the Triat and the countless umbral worlds, spirits, entities and strangeness (like the Dreaming, Shadowlands, Oblivion, Astral Realms, Abyss, the planets and even the Thousand Hells) with their own agendas and plans, and where the concepts and ideas of the Triat never really come into play outside the most general ones.<br /> <br /> Whenever the factions of the WoD encounter the servants of the insane Wyrm in action, they all pretty unequivocally agree that these things are evil, horrible and should be killed and fought (Even the Devil Tigers know that there is no profound wisdom in crazy monsters, so they kill them or force them to serve them instead). What they disagree and discuss philosophically is what can be done with the Wyrm... Is it Evil? Are its servants evil? Can it be healed? Funnily, this same discussion exists in Werewolf, KotE and Mage (check the same page where you saw the discussion on the Tiger, Dragon and the Phoenix).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T06:08:11-07:00","id":451448,"title":"","content":"oh, im not arguing whether or not the wyrm fulfills it's main purpose. even the werewolf core rulebook admits it does.<br /> <br /> that being said is it not strange that for some reason entropy is always the most corrupted part of the trinity? with weaver coming second(and even then many of the things it has done can be considered good for normal humanity).<br /> <br /> the difference is that dragons of the east says that the ebon dragon is good!. and itis only it;'s misguided/corrupted servants doing the nasty stuff.<br /> werewolf(again at least the core rulebook) seems to say the the wyrm is evil even if it does do it's original purpose unintentionally<br /> <br /> plus im not sure if the trinity is supposed to be ,dynamist,stasis,entropy or are just regulating it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T06:19:33-07:00","id":451450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=450684#post450684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, does DtF actually come out and say that the members of the Triat, the vast beings that underlie the Tellurian, are just angels or demons? Blagh. I know that the Paradise Lost narrative was never made to play nice with the other cosmologies of the WoD, but if that is the approach they took, it is riotously stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> None of the cosmologies play nice with each other. The supremacy of the Triat was always the WtA pov, not a universal assumption of every gameline. If you're playing Demon, yes things are assumed to fit into the Miltonian narrative - but that's only if you're playing Demon, it's not saying that's true if you're playing Werewolf.<br /> <br /> *Mage in the distance starts screaming something about different cosmological &quot;paradigms&quot;*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T07:38:32-07:00","id":451507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=451448#post451448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh, im not arguing whether or not the wyrm fulfills it's main purpose. even the werewolf core rulebook admits it does.<br /> <br /> that being said is it not strange that for some reason entropy is always the most corrupted part of the trinity? with weaver coming second(and even then many of the things it has done can be considered good for normal humanity).<br /> <br /> the difference is that dragons of the east says that the ebon dragon is good!. and itis only it;'s misguided/corrupted servants doing the nasty stuff.<br /> werewolf(again at least the core rulebook) seems to say the the wyrm is evil even if it does do it's original purpose unintentionally<br /> <br /> plus im not sure if the trinity is supposed to be ,dynamist,stasis,entropy or are just regulating it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ebon Dragon isn't the Wyrm, and at no point does KotE ever even conflate the two or identify beings associated with the Ebon Dragon as being evil or even slightly misguided (look to your copy of The Thousand Hells, page 17 for everything that KotE has to say about the Wyrm). It's an entity of pure Yin serving as the counterpart to the Scarlet Queen. Those two, like the trinity of Tiger, Phoenix and Dragon, have nothing to do with the Triat. They are concerned with the Daoist principles of Yin and Yang, and are,much smaller than the Wyrm is, conceptually speaking. The closest concept to the SQ and ED in Werewolf would be the divisions of the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T07:50:35-07:00","id":451512,"title":"","content":"i don't know what kindred of the east says(but will check tha page once i find my copy) but dragons of the east seems to explicitly say<br /> <br /> that these are members of the trinity. it says that &quot;tiger is also called the scarlet queen&quot; . will recheck it to make sure. i suppose these mages could just be wrong of course","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T08:03:16-07:00","id":451523,"title":"","content":"Crossover discussion threads seem to wind and went their way here all the time don't they?<br /> <br /> Mark,<br /> <br /> My answer to your OP is that DD uses Torment in a simplified way compared to DtF, because, why not? It's an antagonist book and it's not really designed to make DA devils playable characters. So, the reason that DD has a lid on Torment at 10 is that, even though it's being used as a &quot;power pool&quot; stat, it's really more of a &quot;power stat&quot; sensu stricto, like Pathos, Gnosis, Glamour, etc. It determines the value of that pool an limits it, but, not all Torment 10 are created equal, just like all Wraiths have max Pathos 10: a Deathlord and a wraith that was Reaped yesterday could both have Pathos 10. Joe the Demon From Hell who is possessing my buddy Adelbard can have Torment 10. (Poor, poor Joe.) Belial, the Great Beast, also has Torment 10. Belial can almost certainly use his Torment 10 more effectively than Joe, just like the Deathlord can use his Pathos and Angst more effectively than the newbie wraith.<br /> <br /> Even though DtF Earthbound explicitly does not handle the Archdukes (more handwaving that they're too strong for stats), it does give a really good idea of exactly how powerful Earthbound can get. They all have Torment 10, but their Torment 10 ends up being a different beastie.<br /> <br /> Obviously, DD is just using DtF terms where they work out, and the meanings are not precisely the same between the two, but, as the DtF is informing DD, it seems like the answers are there. With the caveat that DtF is in no way as fully developed a line as the DA, so there are going to be lacunae there as well. Things they just didn't get to. (Like actual rules about Demons and the other two Umbrae, aka how, exactly Demon will elect to stomp all over Werewolf. Like Werewold stomps all over everyone else in a brute force kinda way and Mage does so in an erudite and lawyerly way.) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T08:18:25-07:00","id":451538,"title":"","content":"in dtf there is the mastery background. only the mightiest demons(mostly earthbound or ones still on the abyss i think) have it. whick is why i find the idea of all demons having infinite powerthere strange.<br /> <br /> )which as i just found is strangely also what devil's due says when it explains that resolve is not really &quot;power&quot; )<br /> <br /> unless we are talking about potential infinite power. even then the strongest of mages beat even mastery 5.<br /> <br /> it doesn't help that devil's due has no metaphysical reason of why it works so differently. it really seems to be a retcon of the demon game line","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T13:11:15-07:00","id":451962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=451512#post451512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i don't know what kindred of the east says(but will check tha page once i find my copy) but dragons of the east seems to explicitly say<br /> <br /> that these are members of the trinity. it says that &quot;tiger is also called the scarlet queen&quot; . will recheck it to make sure. i suppose these mages could just be wrong of course</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragons of the East is referring to the ministers of Yin, Yang and the balance between them. This setup is not the same thing as the Triat of Werewolf. It is the setup of the different types of Umbral reflections; the Middle is Yang because it's also known as the Yang World, Dark is Yin because it's also known as the Yin World, and Balance would be the between point of the material realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T06:09:04-07:00","id":452575,"title":"","content":"from dragons of the east page 40.<br /> <br /> tiger is the minister of yang,full of creative and chaotic power. many hengeyokai bear his legacy.<br /> phoenix brings order to the world. also called scarlet queen. though the kuei jin identify her with yang.<br /> the ebon dragon purges the wheel of its flaws so that they do not impede it's turning.<br /> in the second age dragon's ministers tured against him<br /> primal mystics argue that dragon has gone mad and seeks to corrupt the world.<br /> akashics and wu lung argue that his servants are evil because phoenix has him to tightly bound to act.<br /> <br /> personally i think that the truth propably combines elements of both beliefs. none is entirely correct.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T08:42:29-07:00","id":452712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=452575#post452575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> from dragons of the east page 40.<br /> <br /> tiger is the minister of yang,full of creative and chaotic power. many hengeyokai bear his legacy.<br /> phoenix brings order to the world. also called scarlet queen. though the kuei jin identify her with yang.<br /> the ebon dragon purges the wheel of its flaws so that they do not impede it's turning.<br /> in the second age dragon's ministers tured against him<br /> primal mystics argue that dragon has gone mad and seeks to corrupt the world.<br /> akashics and wu lung argue that his servants are evil because phoenix has him to tightly bound to act.<br /> <br /> personally i think that the truth propably combines elements of both beliefs. none is entirely correct.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Dragons of the East is bonkers and seems to have a heavy slant toward legalism, because it ends up ascribing Yin as a destructive or even evil force and equating it with Jhor, which doesn't really fit with any of the other pieces on the table. I think the takeaway here is &quot;don't trust what Mages say, because they hear shit and try to mix it all together in ways that don't make sense.&quot; I suppose it might make sense if you were the Namebreaker in question, but seriously, who wants to understand the worldview of a being that's broken, and trying to fracture everything else in the universe to match their twisted personal vision?<br /> <br /> Just because there are systems of the cosmos that exist doesn't mean that they can be neatly combined together in a single correspondence. There are enough differences from the Triat and the concept of Yin, Yang, and Balance that attempting to combine the two results in a system that can only hold together in the barest sense of the word. Coming together for an instant, and only on paper, is no way to construct a view of the cosmos.<br /> <br /> Edit: Goofed. It's certain schools of Confucianism that draw moral lines on Yin and Yang, not Legalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 03-23-2015, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T09:54:23-07:00","id":452783,"title":"","content":"i am not saying they fit perfecty. hell even trying to reconcile writers mistakes or things they wrote without thinking they implications with the rest of the plot and trying to separate it from things that are part of the &quot;correct&quot; metaphysics(problem being that as much as i may wish it there was rarely any secret plot hidden in the books for us to discover. just freelance writers who can't always know/remember every single thing written in the books)<br /> <br /> there are so many wild inconsistencies it hurts my head thinking about it. that being said for some time ive been trying with mixed success to reconcile the differences between gamelines(or the countless inconsistencies within the same fucking gameline) i think im making some progress but some compromises have to be made. in a month or so i think ill make a thread where ill post the info on the incosistencies ive gathered and what little ive been able to reconcile.<br /> ive seen similar threads in the past with people trying to find ways to do the same. but they were a bit incomplete. mage is of course the worse violator<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 03-22-2015, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T15:33:56-07:00","id":453275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=452783#post452783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i am not saying they fit perfecty. hell even trying to reconcile writers mistakes or things they wrote without thinking they implications with the rest of the plot and trying to separate it from things that are part of the &quot;correct&quot; metaphysics(problem being that as much as i may wish it there was rarely any secret plot hidden in the books for us to discover. just freelance writers who can't always know/remember every single thing written in the books)<br /> <br /> there are so many wild inconsistencies it hurts my head thinking about it. that being said for some time ive been trying with mixed success to reconcile the differences between gamelines(or the countless inconsistencies within the same fucking gameline) i think im making some progress but some compromises have to be made. in a month or so i think ill make a thread where ill post the info on the incosistencies ive gathered and what little ive been able to reconcile.<br /> ive seen similar threads in the past with people trying to find ways to do the same. but they were a bit incomplete. mage is of course the worse violator<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are no inconsistencies. Only different ways of perceiving. Each independent reality is equally true within it's own context. The failure of perception can only be rectified by achieving an ultimate and transcendent perspective. Of course, once achieved, communicating such a perspective to any non-Ascended being is impossible due to the flaws inherent in a non-Ascended existence. <br /> <br /> So... uh,uh, Mage isn't the worst violator, it's the ultimate enabler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T15:43:16-07:00","id":453285,"title":"","content":"it also doesn't help that ascended people sort of,well ascend<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> with the exception of the oracles.<br /> <br /> personally though ,for various reasons i am not sure if i like the fractured cosmos scenario. besides technically speaking it is not necessarily canon.<br /> <br /> by inconsistencies i also mean things like e.g the nature of souls and avatars . is a soul and consciousness one and the same? is a soul the avatar? many books imply this is the case others say so.<br /> if the answer is yes it's like saying that every other being is soulless. <br /> is there one tellurian or many? things like that have different answers depending on the book and player interpretation<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T16:11:16-07:00","id":453323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=453275#post453275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are no inconsistencies. Only different ways of perceiving. Each independent reality is equally true within it's own context. The failure of perception can only be rectified by achieving an ultimate and transcendent perspective. Of course, once achieved, communicating such a perspective to any non-Ascended being is impossible due to the flaws inherent in a non-Ascended existence.<br /> <br /> So... uh,uh, Mage isn't the worst violator, it's the ultimate enabler.</div> </div> </div> </div>How convenient that the &quot;solution&quot; is found in Mage.<br /> <br /> Again, Mage can only explain Mage. It doesn't actually have a transcendent point of view that can fit everything, it just talks a big game and goes back to steampunk cruisers and Space 1889 fighting futuristic starships past Jupiter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T18:54:43-07:00","id":453561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=452783#post452783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in a month or so i think ill make a thread where ill post the info on the incosistencies ive gathered and what little ive been able to reconcile. ive seen similar threads in the past with people trying to find ways to do the same. but they were a bit incomplete. mage is of course the worse violator<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't bother. It's a waste of your time. We've known it for decades now and we even used to discuss it on usenet with vitriol and gusto and confusion and zeal. Nowadays most people here are well aware of what they are getting into and tend to keep to what they feel is the most comfortable. And the newbies? Poor newbies shouldn't ever see the warts of oWoD as their introduction to the game(s).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T19:21:22-07:00","id":453622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=453323#post453323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How convenient that the &quot;solution&quot; is found in Mage.<br /> <br /> Again, Mage can only explain Mage. It doesn't actually have a transcendent point of view that can fit everything, it just talks a big game and goes back to steampunk cruisers and Space 1889 fighting futuristic starships past Jupiter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mark said Mage was the worst violator. It's not. No more or less than any of the other games. Actually any more than Werewolf, which is just as dominatey with it's view of everything. At least a Mage a can say, &quot;That may be true for you, but...&quot; Werewolves just slam everything willy-nilly into the categories intrinsic to that game. Which works VERY WELL for it, but doesn't really fit anyone else very well <br /> <br /> Which means both games are cosmologically exactly what they are in most other ways. There is no way that they can play nice at the level of harmonization. Except for the mages to get all haughty. Which isn't playing nice really. <br /> <br /> I've run a dozen mage games over the last two decades plus. At least. And never, ever had a steampunk cruiser, or anything remotely resembling Space 1889. Though one, and only one, was close... the futuristic starships thing. So, no. <br /> <br /> There might be something to be said for some possibilities for more ease of interlocking with a Demon-Hunter-Vampire-Wraith with, possibly, KoE and Mummy the final. If you want to look at things at exactly the right angles. Guess there's no reason not to add Changeling to that, but that's simply because Changeling doesn't really fit or not fit. It just kinda is. <br /> <br /> Of course, THAT potential possible maybe uneven continuum doesn't play well with Werewolf or Mage.... so.... no joy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:05:43-07:00","id":454525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=450807#post450807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Triat HAS to exist as the fundamental underpinning of the cosmos for all the games, it's just privileging the mythology of Werewolf and slopping that all over the other games. Which is doing exactly the same thing people say Demon does....</div> </div> </div> </div>With the added bonus that it's privileging a treehugging ALL PROGRESS=BAD! mythology practiced by a few thousand shapeshifters in-setting and as far as I'm aware isn't based on any real-world religion of note, as opposed to DtF at least being based on the religions that have been the dominant cultural paradigm both in-setting and in the real world for the last millenium or so and are currently practiced in some form by about 55% of the world's 7 billiion people. Including what I would bet is at least a plurality of White Wolf's customers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:25:36-07:00","id":454557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=454525#post454525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the added bonus that it's privileging a treehugging ALL PROGRESS=BAD! mythology practiced by a few thousand shapeshifters in-setting and as far as I'm aware isn't based on any real-world religion of note, as opposed to DtF at least being based on the religions that have been the dominant cultural paradigm both in-setting and in the real world for the last millenium or so and are currently practiced in some form by about 55% of the world's 7 billiion people. Including what I would bet is at least a plurality of White Wolf's customers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, isn't really based on much in the way of werewolf mythology that came before the game. Sure, the Tribes are based on some bits of werewolf mythology here and there, but the furry-ecoterrorist-filled-with-righteous-indignation was pretty much invented by White Wolf, largely out of whole cloth. You start with wolves=wild and extrapolate the structure from there, then cherry-pick through folklore, mythology and fiction to fill in the Tribes here and there, make up the rest through some cool metaphorical linkages and some taxonomy. That's BRILLIANT. So brilliant in fact that they actually CREATED a werewolf trope that has become widespread. But it is mostly made up for the game proper. It is less &quot;grounded&quot; than most of the other games because of that disconnect in the linkage (or link- e.g. Vampires to Caine, which was made before them but they sure as Hell ran with it) between the constructed game mythology and that-which-came-before. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T11:05:06-07:00","id":454610,"title":"","content":"personally i think it's easy to reconcile mage with werewolf.<br /> <br /> 1. werewolf teaches the world is animistic. that is, a telephone has a spirit.<br /> mage agrees. the middle umbra the spirits of objects etc all exist. no matter what the technocracy says. what people sometines forget is that the consenus influences but does not<b> define</b> reality.<br /> plus there are cosmological constants. the earth was always round. and it was always far older than 7000 years old. just ask hinduism. though we could debate the exact age.<br /> <br /> from what i know of it a minority of werewolves seem to believe that that gaia is &quot;just&quot; a celestine. the majority obviously disagrees.but even they admit her most direct manifestation is the spirit of earth. other than that it's just faith that this isn't so. besides werewolveswere mage with a specific idea in mind and this was not&quot;explorers of the true nature reality&quot;<br /> in effect many of their believsare.. simplistic or at the very least they have a narrow focus. not unlike mummy or setites narrow view of the universe.<br /> <br /> i can't see how yin is not if not the same then at the very least very similar with entropy. etc.<br /> <br /> not all fera think that progress is bad but those who do are not alone. many mages for one reason or the other share the sentiment.<br /> <br /> demon the fallen is only partially based in abrahamic religions.<br /> <br /> try convincing your priest that&quot; lucifer created modern christianity&quot; and see what the response is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T12:09:42-07:00","id":454700,"title":"","content":"RE: Yin and Yang and the Triat<br /> <br /> Yin is stillness, darkness, potential, cold, and a number of other things. It is nourishment and support. It's intuition and negotiation, ultimately indirect. Yang is direct and active. A candle is fire as yin. A wildfire is fire as yang. Also, they represent two different sexes. In Werewolf parlance, both would be Wyld, or perhaps both potential sides of each member of the Triat. After all, both have the capacity to be active and passive; the Wyrm has monsters for the direct approach and corruption for the indirect, after all. This distinction is present in the Kumo, incidentally, though it also has some... tangles to it (sunglasses, Meet the New Boss clip) since the ones that are killcrazy appear to be Yin-aspected, but their attunements are a matter of appetite, rather than approach. Marawa's Brood are destructive and cruel and prey upon the passive; the Blessed of Rati are big on talk and seduction and prey upon the active. The Chosen of Nareau have their pick of approach and victim. This is taking on the opposite to defeat the main.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the other ramifications of the associations in DotE are that men are of the Wyld and women are of the Wyrm which would be a new dimensions of &quot;holy shit, can you stop, take a breath, and listen to yourself?&quot; even if you ignored the above issues. On a slightly less controversial note, it would also insinuate that water and metal are Wyrmish and that wood and fire are Wyldish; problematic, but in a somewhat absurd way, rather than one with super unfortunate implications.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=454557#post454557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, isn't really based on much in the way of werewolf mythology that came before the game. Sure, the Tribes are based on some bits of werewolf mythology here and there, but the furry-ecoterrorist-filled-with-righteous-indignation was pretty much invented by White Wolf, largely out of whole cloth. You start with wolves=wild and extrapolate the structure from there, then cherry-pick through folklore, mythology and fiction to fill in the Tribes here and there, make up the rest through some cool metaphorical linkages and some taxonomy. That's BRILLIANT. So brilliant in fact that they actually CREATED a werewolf trope that has become widespread. But it is mostly made up for the game proper. It is less &quot;grounded&quot; than most of the other games because of that disconnect in the linkage (or link- e.g. Vampires to Caine, which was made before them but they sure as Hell ran with it) between the constructed game mythology and that-which-came-before.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that being an original creation of WW ought to get it more swinging weight in WW's settings than less, if you're going to phrase things that way. It's their own synthesis of ideas, their baby; they should commit to promoting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T12:34:09-07:00","id":454725,"title":"","content":"in that case maybe these 3 ministers are the trinity.. but eastern splats are wrong to attribute yin and yang to them. or at least it's more complicated.<br /> <br /> for instance the ebon dragon/wyrm is associatedwith entropy. it'sfair to assume that theire is nothing more entropic that the underworld.<br /> <br /> though in 1000 hels it says that the connection of yomi to the underworld is called ebon path while the yang path is the one bringig them with contact with malfeas.<br /> <br /> which actually is in the deep umbra though it's implied that the labyrinth/oblivion is actually beneath everything!<br /> <br /> one interpretation may be that the wyrm may influence the underworld because it's unsociated with entropy.<br /> <br /> the wyld may then influence the middle umbra.<br /> <br /> with maybe the weaver influencing the astral realm?<br /> <br /> with noone having complete control over these areas of course. they are just &quot;similar&quot;<br /> <br /> amd then there is darkmother and oblivion...god it's just maddening!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T12:51:10-07:00","id":454753,"title":"","content":"Yeah - the Ministers map easily to the Metaphysical Trinity. Despite some superficial similarities, the Trinity <b><i>doesn't</i></b> at all map to the Triat. In particular, Pattern contains elements of beneficial stability, continuity, and parental nurturing which are completely absent from the Weaver. Dragon-Minister contains elements of law and consequence - the Wyrm (as corrupter or destroyer) only acknowledges the absolute natural law of eventual death. Mapping Yang onto the Phoenix Minister doesn't make a whole ton of sense, either. There are similarities, but I have yet to see a means of reconciling Werewolf's ecological animist cosmology with Mage that doesn't leave one of the two very much the junior partner.<br /> <br /> Imagine a venn diagram in which the traits of the Wyrm, the Ebon Dragon, and the Dragon Minister share some overlap, but aren't the same circles. Dragon-Minister is performing a very different task in Mage's thematic cosmology. There are hints of intersection and cross-over, but those are suggestive or iconic, ways that each game dips into a shared well of common symbols and ideas, not a consistent singular cosmology that can be documented in a straightforward fashion. Trying to make sense of the game lines shared symbol set as if the same symbols express the <i>same</i> things in each game line is always going to be doomed to frustration. They express <i>similar </i>things, as suited for the themes and intents of each game line.<br /> <br /> &quot;Dragonlike thing what is involved in destruction&quot; is basically the WoD equivalent of a cape in superhero comics; we understand that not everyone wearing a cape is the same character but understand that the cape is part of an artistic decision to communicate some basic ideas about what sort of character we are seeing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T13:16:51-07:00","id":454785,"title":"","content":"i could be reading what youre saying wrong but if not then essentially you mean that the ministers are less corrupt than their &quot;western&quot; counter parts. or that they are interpreted as such.<br /> <br /> i also see a serious case of anthropotheism in the case of the ministers.<br /> <br /> essentially my point is that since they can't be reconciled perfectly the next best thingis saying that each side made some mistakes. after all no one can have a perfect view ofthe universe.<br /> <br /> think of it like what happens when a divided congress passes the new years budget<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T13:33:10-07:00","id":454799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=454785#post454785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i could be reading what youre saying wrong but if not then essentially you mean that the ministers are less corrupt than their &quot;western&quot; counter parts. or that they are interpreted as such.essentially my point is that since they can't be reconciled perfectly the next best thingis saying that each side made some mistakes. after all no one can have a perfect view ofthe universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, from my perspective that's the wrong way to look at it. The Wyrm isn't the Western &quot;version&quot; of the Dragon-Minister; in a universe where the Dragon-Minister exists, the Wyrm either doesn't exist, or the thing that is called the Wyrm has different traits (and is fulfilling a different purpose in-universe and for the players/ST) than the Wyrm does in a Werewolf game. Similarly, in a Werewolf game, the thing that Stargazers call the Dragon-Minister isn't the same as what that name would &quot;mean&quot; in a Mage game. The Ministers are more invested in human concepts because the point of the Triat (and of Werewolf's cosmology) is that humanity isn't as important as it imagines itself to be, on a cosmic scale; Mage's argument runs rather the opposite (in fact, most of humanity, in Mage, <i>underestimates </i>its own value<i>.</i>)<br /> <br /> What I am trying to say is that you are looking at two pictures, each of which depicts a dude in a cape teaming up with a dude with a bow and arrow.<br /> <br /> One of them is Thor and Hawkeye, the other one is Superman and Green Arrow.<br /> <br /> &quot;Where is Superman's hammer?&quot; is not a sensible question to ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T13:54:16-07:00","id":454807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=454725#post454725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in that case maybe these 3 ministers are the trinity.. but eastern splats are wrong to attribute yin and yang to them. or at least it's more complicated.<br /> <br /> for instance the ebon dragon/wyrm is associatedwith entropy. it'sfair to assume that theire is nothing more entropic that the underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ebon Dragon is a being of utmost stillness, indirectness and passivity and it reaches into the Underworld but isn't the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> though in 1000 hels it says that the connection of yomi to the underworld is called ebon path while the yang path is the one bringig them with contact with malfeas.<br /> <br /> which actually is in the deep umbra though it's implied that the labyrinth/oblivion is actually beneath everything! </div> </div> </div>Malfeas is a Near Umbral Realm. It isn't in the Deep Umbra, or in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> one interpretation may be that the wyrm may influence the underworld because it's unsociated with entropy.<br /> <br /> the wyld may then influence the middle umbra.<br /> <br /> with maybe the weaver influencing the astral realm? </div> </div> </div>No. The Middle Umbra is in a threeway tug of war between the entire Triat. They don't really care so much about the other reaches of the Umbra. The Astral is likely much the same; in past editions, it was the stomping ground of Mokole, as far as Werewolf was concerned anyway, and the Mind of Gaia often had unwelcome invaders, such as memory-eaters..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> with noone having complete control over these areas of course. they are just &quot;similar&quot;<br /> <br /> amd then there is darkmother and oblivion...god it's just maddening! </div> </div> </div>That's why you don't take a hit of everything at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T14:42:03-07:00","id":454883,"title":"","content":"are you sure malfeas is in the near umbra? white wolf wiki says deep.<br /> <br /> my point was that western and eastern supernaturals may view them through different lens and that each perspective has at least some amount of validity.<br /> <br /> at the very least this is what the writers of dragons of the east seemed to be thinking.<br /> <br /> not that it makes it necessarily correct just as with the somewhat contradictory explanations on the nature of avatars<br /> <br /> it's just that i personally like the dragons of east version.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T16:56:58-07:00","id":455027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=454700#post454700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that being an original creation of WW ought to get it more swinging weight in WW's settings than less, if you're going to phrase things that way. It's their own synthesis of ideas, their baby; they should commit to promoting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, they should re-write Vampire to have them all be Wyrm creatures? And Mage to have them all be &quot;Namers&quot; with some nebulous, ill-defined powers that must be less than those of Gaia's Chosen? Delete Wraith, Demon and probably Hunter too because they don't have a animistic apocalyptic spiritualist focus? (I mean, really who cares about dead monkeys that can't figure out how to reincarnate like REAL people, us, the Garou)? <br /> <br /> Again, Changeling always seems to work, because it doesn't really. Which is it's own kind of brilliance.<br /> <br /> Since the game lines are supposedly based on historical/mythical/legendary/fictional/folklore archetypes, then, no, you shouldn't be committed to promoting it over and above the others as the One Ring of CWOD cosmologies. Werewolf put the cart before the horse, and lo and behold it worked, but that doesn't make it superior. In fact, that is probably one of the things that makes it so very hard to fit it in alongside the others. It can work just as fine being on top. You just have to answer all the above questions &quot;Yes&quot; and be working with a group of fellow players who are okay with playing those kind of vampires (more squick, less LeStat or Dracula), those kinds of Mages, etc., etc. <br /> <br /> All the games get equal swinging weight. So you have to do the cross-over dance and you can't really find a a way to find an inflection point where it all balances out but everything still gets to stay itself. You have to pick and choose how they fit together and you are going to have to bend, break, delete, forget and forge to make even some kind of half-assed compromise. Whittle down the number of dancers and you make your job easier. Pick one to be the normative consciousness and you make your job easier. <br /> <br /> The closest to a &quot;completely original&quot; WW creation is Exalted. That's their actual baby. Removed enough from any source material to be its own thing and no close connections or analogues to an alleged external/older background of source materials. Sure you CAN play the matching game, but it's just for giggles mostly and it doesn't really affect Exalted all that much if these guys are supposedly going to be Vamps, these Werewolves, etc. And that was pretty much explicitly abandoned. And they ARE committed to throwing all the weight they can behind it, the fans want all that and more (and a bag of chips). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T17:07:41-07:00","id":455035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=454883#post454883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">are you sure malfeas is in the near umbra? white wolf wiki says deep.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only white wolf wiki that's up right now is unofficial, and all the books put it in the same list of Near Realms with The Scar, Pangaea, Wolfhome, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> my point was that western and eastern supernaturals may view them through different lens and that each perspective has at least some amount of validity.<br /> <br /> at the very least this is what the writers of dragons of the east seemed to be thinking.<br /> <br /> not that it makes it necessarily correct just as with the somewhat contradictory explanations on the nature of avatars<br /> <br /> it's just that i personally like the dragons of east version.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Hengeyokai and KotE did not endorse the same split, though, so what was described in DotE isn't actually a universal thing, just something that Namebreakers think. It could very easily have come about from hearing Demon People talking about the Ebon Dragon and the Beast Courts talking about the Centipede, and then playing a really serious game of telephone. Add in some questions to irritable hungry dead or shapeshifters that don't like telling mages anything, and you're going to end up with some seriously distorted views of the world. After all, the Dragon Wizards also claim to be descended from dragons, but they don't typically voice those claims around Middle Dragons, because they might just be lies and pretensions that would offend the Mokole, in addition to the Mokole's ancestors and all future Mokole of the same lineage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T11:27:15-07:00","id":456028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=455035#post455035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only white wolf wiki that's up right now is unofficial, and all the books put it in the same list of Near Realms with The Scar, Pangaea, Wolfhome, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Book of Worlds places Malfeas as the Shenti of Entropy out in the Deep Umbra somewhere, like Autochthonia is the Shenti of Stasis occupying Earth's orbit on the opposite side of the sun.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T15:52:26-07:00","id":456281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=456028#post456028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Book of Worlds places Malfeas as the Shenti of Entropy out in the Deep Umbra somewhere, like Autochthonia is the Shenti of Stasis occupying Earth's orbit on the opposite side of the sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>No way, no how. Mage Deep Umbra is what every other game refers to as &quot;outer space&quot;, which is not where you find Malfeas in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Oddly, W20 Umbra also places it in the Near Umbra chapter, whereas W20 Book of the Wyrm seems to place it in the Deep Umbra (Werewolf Deep Umbra, not Mage Deep Umbra). Umbra Revised had it in the Near Umbra, with notes that it might have once been in the Deep Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T16:02:20-07:00","id":456290,"title":"","content":"what's the ifference between the 2 deep umbras?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T16:49:38-07:00","id":456361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=456290#post456290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what's the ifference between the 2 deep umbras?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage Deep Umbra is all of what we would, in real life, call &quot;space outside of the Asteroid Belt&quot;. Werewolf Deep Umbra is a bizarre otherworld like an Umbra beyond the Umbra (prior to W20, it was what Mage called the High Umbra and then some)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T02:51:33-07:00","id":456673,"title":"","content":"The nature of Malfeas in Werewolf has actually changed somewhat over the years. In the early days it was explicitly in the Deep Umbra (Umbra: Velvet Shadow page 12). It later seemed to be moving closer to Earth (Umbra page 73), joining the Near Realms, which is where W20 locates it (Umbra W20 page 43). W20 also notes that the Black Spiral in Malfeas leads to the Wyrm's (unnamed) lair in the Deep Umbra (Umbra W20 page 105). Book of the Wyrm 1e (page 49) confirms that Malfeas is in the Deep Umbra, as does Book of the Wyrm 2e (page 36). Book of the Wyrm W20 also locates Malfeas in the Deep Umbra (pp 14, 21-23), mirroring BotW2e, despite the text in Umbra W20 that locates it as a Near Realm. How you reconcile this is up to the individual ST, of course.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the nature of the Deep Umbra in Mage, it has also changed over the years. Initially, the Deep Umbra was just the realm that lay beyond the Horizon (or Membrane, in Werewolf parlance). How you perceived it depended on your paradigm. For technologically-minded mages, it was deep space. For the mystically-inclined it was a bizarre otherworld, an Umbra beyond the Umbra or the Void. For the Sons of Ether, it was Etherspace. See Book of Worlds, pp 137-138 and page 157. (The latter page also tells us that, according to Mage, Malfeas is in the Deep Umbra). Infinite Tapestry expands on this, giving us multiple Horizons. According to that book (pp 10-11), the First Horizon corresponds to Earth's upper atmosphere and is the limit of Earthly reality. After this, the True Horizon extends out to the Asteroid Belt. Here the paradigm-distinctions from Book of Worlds still apply - to technomancers it's space, to Etherites it's Etherspace, to mystics it's outside of Earthly reality and home to infinite possibilities. Horizon Realms are located here. Finally, the Far Horizon, at the Asteroid Belt, is the barrier to the Deep Umbra. Beyond this lies the Void, known as the Deep Universe to technomancers. Out there, all the laws of reality break down, technological, mystical or otherwise and all mages are out of their element.<br /> <br /> So (the shifting location of Malfeas aside), the chief differences between the Deep Umbras in Werewolf and Mage are down to the location of the Horizon/Membrane. Werewolf (and pre-Revised Mage) doesn't really have the multiple gradations of Horizon that Revised Mage does - there's just a Membrane/Horizon that separates Near from Deep Umbras. The Deep Umbras are the same in both games, more or less. Mage allows for paradigm-based distinctions in how the Deep Umbra appears, but this isn't a factor in Werewolf. Both games also have aspects of the Deep Umbra leaking into the Near Umbra (Reaches and Shenti). As with all things WoD, there are inconsistencies. Treat these as opportunities for customisation, rather than obstacles to enjoyable play <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T07:52:11-07:00","id":456848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=456673#post456673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nature of Malfeas in Werewolf has actually changed somewhat over the years. In the early days it was explicitly in the Deep Umbra (Umbra: Velvet Shadow page 12). It later seemed to be moving closer to Earth (Umbra page 73), joining the Near Realms, which is where W20 locates it (Umbra W20 page 43). W20 also notes that the Black Spiral in Malfeas leads to the Wyrm's (unnamed) lair in the Deep Umbra (Umbra W20 page 105). Book of the Wyrm 1e (page 49) confirms that Malfeas is in the Deep Umbra, as does Book of the Wyrm 2e (page 36). Book of the Wyrm W20 also locates Malfeas in the Deep Umbra (pp 14, 21-23), mirroring BotW2e, despite the text in Umbra W20 that locates it as a Near Realm. How you reconcile this is up to the individual ST, of course.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the nature of the Deep Umbra in Mage, it has also changed over the years. Initially, the Deep Umbra was just the realm that lay beyond the Horizon (or Membrane, in Werewolf parlance). How you perceived it depended on your paradigm. For technologically-minded mages, it was deep space. For the mystically-inclined it was a bizarre otherworld, an Umbra beyond the Umbra or the Void. For the Sons of Ether, it was Etherspace. See Book of Worlds, pp 137-138 and page 157. (The latter page also tells us that, according to Mage, Malfeas is in the Deep Umbra). Infinite Tapestry expands on this, giving us multiple Horizons. According to that book (pp 10-11), the First Horizon corresponds to Earth's upper atmosphere and is the limit of Earthly reality. After this, the True Horizon extends out to the Asteroid Belt. Here the paradigm-distinctions from Book of Worlds still apply - to technomancers it's space, to Etherites it's Etherspace, to mystics it's outside of Earthly reality and home to infinite possibilities. Horizon Realms are located here. Finally, the Far Horizon, at the Asteroid Belt, is the barrier to the Deep Umbra. Beyond this lies the Void, known as the Deep Universe to technomancers. Out there, all the laws of reality break down, technological, mystical or otherwise and all mages are out of their element.<br /> <br /> So (the shifting location of Malfeas aside), the chief differences between the Deep Umbras in Werewolf and Mage are down to the location of the Horizon/Membrane. Werewolf (and pre-Revised Mage) doesn't really have the multiple gradations of Horizon that Revised Mage does - there's just a Membrane/Horizon that separates Near from Deep Umbras. The Deep Umbras are the same in both games, more or less. Mage allows for paradigm-based distinctions in how the Deep Umbra appears, but this isn't a factor in Werewolf. Both games also have aspects of the Deep Umbra leaking into the Near Umbra (Reaches and Shenti). As with all things WoD, there are inconsistencies. Treat these as opportunities for customisation, rather than obstacles to enjoyable play <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's still a notable difference in that the Deep Umbra is not something that is gone to instead of space in Werewolf. It coexists with the concept of a vast universe as understood by real world cosmology. In Mage, you go to one or the other, in Werewolf, you could go to both, though it's really ill-advised to step sideways from the Aetherial Realm and back into the physical world if you don't have some manner of protection from a hostile environment, and unlikely that most Garou or Fera are going to end up on a shuttle mission. Also, missions into deep space don't require magic(k) or any form of spiritual attunement, what with outer space being a part of the much larger physical realm of Werewolf and not the sharply limited non-mystic(k) existence of Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T08:02:19-07:00","id":456873,"title":"","content":"True, Werewolf doesn't really address mundane space as a destination for adventuring, concentrating instead on the Deep Umbra as a place <i>not</i> to go, if you can help it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T08:07:31-07:00","id":456875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=456361#post456361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mage Deep Umbra is all of what we would, in real life, call &quot;space outside of the Asteroid Belt&quot;. Werewolf Deep Umbra is a bizarre otherworld like an Umbra beyond the 