mind 5 spirit 5 for deem umbra not dream umbra. my bad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T11:27:09-07:00","id":457075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=456281#post456281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No way, no how. Mage Deep Umbra is what every other game refers to as &quot;outer space&quot;, which is not where you find Malfeas in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Oddly, W20 Umbra also places it in the Near Umbra chapter, whereas W20 Book of the Wyrm seems to place it in the Deep Umbra (Werewolf Deep Umbra, not Mage Deep Umbra). Umbra Revised had it in the Near Umbra, with notes that it might have once been in the Deep Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, I get that you view everything through a Werewolf-colored lens and are prone to &quot;Nuh-uh!&quot;-ing concepts from other games, but all the books demonstrably DO NOT agree on where Malfeas is located as you maintained earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T11:35:50-07:00","id":457084,"title":"","content":"Why can't it be in both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T14:43:31-07:00","id":457311,"title":"","content":"As Umbral realms aren't really proper locations, its quite feasible that it might be entered from either. Mind you, what kind of sick puppy would want to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T16:55:07-07:00","id":457420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/433151-in-dark-ages-devil-due-are-all-demons-equally-strong?p=457075#post457075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dude, I get that you view everything through a Werewolf-colored lens and are prone to &quot;Nuh-uh!&quot;-ing concepts from other games, but all the books demonstrably DO NOT agree on where Malfeas is located as you maintained earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't even agree with each other! Some do put it in the Near Umbra. Some don't. It was lumped into the Near Realms for all of Revised, and that's where it pretty much stayed until W20... which still has it in the same chapter as the Near Realms in W20 Velvet Shadow, rather than the section on the Deep Umbra. I don't think that I'm unjustified here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T19:14:08-07:00","id":457585,"title":"","content":"Just my 2 cents: where something is exactly in the Umbra is kind of a hard question to answer (even from an out of game perspective). I've always read Malfeas to be in the &quot;near&quot; Umbra since it's always been a near Umbral realm (I started playing WoD with Werewolf and Vampire, and Vampire doesn't care about the Umbra). But since distance/location isn't definite in the Umbra, the term &quot;near&quot; doesn't really mean much. There are certainly going to be multiple entrances. And especially with the concept of it moving closer to Earth (sort of), it would have had to at some point bridged the across the near and deep Umbras. There is nothing to say that still doesn't. But as someone stated, each ST ends up having to decide these sort of things for themselves, for any individual game they plan to run. A lot of the time, this sort of discussion doesn't even come up in game, and only serves to inform the ST of how the setting works for themselves.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}